# 🚀 Difference Array (Range Update Technique)

> **One of the most important array techniques for interviews.**
>
> Use it whenever the problem asks:
>
> - Perform **many range updates**
> - Add/subtract a value on an interval `[l, r]`
> - Apply multiple operations, then print the final array

---

# 📌 Problem Motivation

Suppose

```text
arr = [0,0,0,0,0]
```

Operations

```text
Add +2 to indices [1,3]

Add +3 to indices [2,4]

Add -1 to indices [0,2]
```

Naive solution

```text
for every operation
    update every element in range
```

Time Complexity

```text
O(Q × N)
```

If

```text
N = 10^5
Q = 10^5
```

then

```text
10^10
```

operations ❌

Too slow.

---

# 💡 Main Intuition

Instead of updating **every element**,

update only

- where the effect **starts**
- where the effect **stops**

Think of pouring water.

```
Normal Update

0 0 0 0 0

+5 on [1,3]

0 5 5 5 0
```

Instead of filling every bucket,

just place

```
+5 at start

-5 after end
```

```
0  +5  0  0  -5
```

Later,

take prefix sum.

The +5 automatically flows forward.

---

# 📌 Difference Array Concept

Suppose

```text
arr

5 8 10 7 6
```

Difference array

```text
diff[0] = arr[0]

diff[i] = arr[i]-arr[i-1]
```

Example

```
arr

5 8 10 7 6

diff

5 3 2 -3 -1
```

Notice

```
5

5+3=8

8+2=10

10-3=7

7-1=6
```

Prefix sum reconstructs original array.

---

# ⭐ Important Observation

Difference array stores

> **How much value changes at every index.**

Not the actual values.

---

# Range Update

Suppose

```
Add +5 on [2,5]
```

Instead of

```
0 0 5 5 5 5 0 0
```

Store

```
Index

0 1 2 3 4 5 6 7

Diff

0 0 +5 0 0 0 -5 0
```

Meaning

```
Start adding +5 here

↓

Stop adding after index 5
```

---

# Algorithm

For every update

```
(l,r,val)
```

Do

```python
diff[l] += val

if r+1 < n:
    diff[r+1] -= val
```

After processing all updates,

take prefix sum.

---

# Why Does This Work?

Suppose

```
+10 on [1,4]
```

Difference array

```
0 10 0 0 0 -10
```

Prefix

```
0

10

10

10

10

0
```

Exactly what we wanted.

